{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ypr2fg","slideIndex":4,"text":"Data: evidence/garak/*.report.jsonl and evidence/summary.json. The two DAN detectors score one shared answer, not two separate tests. A DAN acknowledgement does not prove harmful generation. Normalised search removes non-letters and flags candidates, not semantically verified extra attacks. The remaining protected candidate formats quoted attack text as a numbered list. The descriptive Wilson 95% interval for 0/32 extends to 10.7%; garak's all-zero bootstrap interval must not be interpreted as zero risk."}
