{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gxnqqz","slideIndex":5,"text":"Source: evidence/paired/responses.jsonl and summary.json. There are 24 attacks and 24 benign prompts per mode. Filter confusion matrix TP=8, FP=8, FN=16, TN=16. Its classification accuracy is 50%, equal to an always-allow classifier on this balanced set. All eight false positives arise in twelve educational security prompts. Ordinary task matching normalises punctuation/case but requires a strict full answer. Response-time means pool these 48 requests, excluding warm-up. The filter speeds refusals, not the model itself."}
